{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00653",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.0,
      "end_seconds": 4.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Mr Chaudhry? Mr Rashid Chaudhry, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.92,
      "end_seconds": 12.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Yes, that is correct. Good morning, Doctor, and thank you for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.13,
      "end_seconds": 20.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "My pleasure. And who has come along with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 21.2,
      "end_seconds": 33.15,
      "duration_seconds": 11.95,
      "text": "I'm Nadia, his daughter. I take him to dialysis most weeks, so I see what goes on at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.93,
      "end_seconds": 50.17,
      "duration_seconds": 16.24,
      "text": "That's very helpful to have. So, Mr Chaudhry, the unit tells me you've been struggling with the fluid limit. Tell me about it in your own words."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.6,
      "end_seconds": 65.12,
      "duration_seconds": 13.52,
      "text": "Yes. I confess I find it very difficult. I am thirsty almost all of the time, and I try to be disciplined, but it is a real struggle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.37,
      "end_seconds": 73.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.46,
      "text": "Thirsty almost all of the time. That sounds exhausting. When is it at its worst?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.33,
      "end_seconds": 83.65,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "The long gap over the weekend. By Sunday evening I could drink the tap dry."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 84.36,
      "end_seconds": 96.59,
      "duration_seconds": 12.23,
      "text": "He keeps a glass by his chair, Doctor, and it ends up empty. Then his ankles blow up by Monday morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.43,
      "end_seconds": 105.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "Ankles swelling by Monday. Is that how it seems to you, Mr Chaudhry?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.66,
      "end_seconds": 116.39,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "Quite so. They are rather swollen on Mondays, and my shoes become a trial."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.05,
      "end_seconds": 128.45,
      "duration_seconds": 10.4,
      "text": "Swollen ankles at the end of the long gap. Is there anything else, during the dialysis itself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.43,
      "end_seconds": 140.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "Cramps, occasionally. In the calves, towards the last hour. They are quite painful, though they pass."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.5,
      "end_seconds": 154.33,
      "duration_seconds": 12.83,
      "text": "Cramps in the last hour of the session, thank you. Let me ask about a few other things. Any chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.95,
      "end_seconds": 157.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "No, none."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.38,
      "end_seconds": 165.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Any trouble breathing when you lie flat at night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.86,
      "end_seconds": 172.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "No, I sleep perfectly well flat, with one pillow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.33,
      "end_seconds": 177.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "And any itching of the skin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.64,
      "end_seconds": 181.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "No, not at present."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.65,
      "end_seconds": 189.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "That's all good news. Now your background. How long have the kidneys been failing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.33,
      "end_seconds": 210.36,
      "duration_seconds": 20.03,
      "text": "Kidney failure for six years now. I was told it came from the high blood pressure, which I have had for twenty years. I also have gout, which flares up now and then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.03,
      "end_seconds": 217.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "And the access for your dialysis, how was that arranged?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.04,
      "end_seconds": 226.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "I had a fistula put in my arm, four years ago. It works very well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.98,
      "end_seconds": 233.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Good. And what tablets are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.92,
      "end_seconds": 247.71,
      "duration_seconds": 11.79,
      "text": "Sevelamer, 800 milligrams with meals, for the phosphate. Amlodipine, 5 milligrams once a day. And folic acid, 5 milligrams in the morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 249.31,
      "end_seconds": 256.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "I fill his pill box on Sundays, so I know where everything stands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.63,
      "end_seconds": 273.18,
      "duration_seconds": 15.55,
      "text": "Lovely, Nadia. So that's sevelamer with meals, amlodipine once a day, and folic acid in the morning. Are you allergic to anything, Mr Chaudhry? Any allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.62,
      "end_seconds": 279.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "No, I have no allergies, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 280.55,
      "end_seconds": 292.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.39,
      "text": "Dad, what about that antibiotic last year, in the hospital? You had a bad reaction to it. I don't remember which one it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.75,
      "end_seconds": 303.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "I do not recall any such thing. I think you may be mistaken, Nadia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 304.9,
      "end_seconds": 310.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Maybe. But the nurse did stop it, I remember that much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.25,
      "end_seconds": 327.51,
      "duration_seconds": 14.26,
      "text": "Let's keep both in mind for now. Mr Chaudhry recalls no allergies, Nadia remembers a reaction to an antibiotic, and we won't settle it today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.07,
      "end_seconds": 331.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Very well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.91,
      "end_seconds": 339.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "Now let me have a look at your ankles, if I may."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.92,
      "end_seconds": 343.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "By all means."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.12,
      "end_seconds": 355.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "There's definite puffiness at the ankles, and it dents when I press with my thumb."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.9,
      "end_seconds": 360.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.97,
      "end_seconds": 389.45,
      "duration_seconds": 28.48,
      "text": "It's what we'd expect when fluid builds up over the long weekend gap. I can't rule out that your target weight on dialysis needs adjusting too, so we'll keep that in mind. Let me say it back: the thirst drives the drinking, the drinking builds the fluid, and the fluid shows in your ankles and your cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.86,
      "end_seconds": 394.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 396.48,
      "end_seconds": 414.92,
      "duration_seconds": 18.44,
      "text": "A few practical things. Use a small cup, not a glass. Suck on ice chips or a sugar-free sweet when the thirst bites. Go easy on salt, because salt makes you thirstier. And spread your allowance through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 416.89,
      "end_seconds": 420.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "He does love his pickles, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 423.15,
      "end_seconds": 424.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Nadia, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.64,
      "end_seconds": 439.38,
      "duration_seconds": 13.74,
      "text": "Pickles are salt in disguise, Mr Chaudhry, so perhaps weekends only for now. So: small cup, ice chips, less salt, spread it out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.35,
      "end_seconds": 442.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "I shall certainly try."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 445.17,
      "end_seconds": 462.04,
      "duration_seconds": 16.87,
      "text": "If the swelling isn't better by next week, come and see me again. And do tell the dialysis nurses about the cramps, they can often adjust things during the session."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 463.72,
      "end_seconds": 468.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. You have been most kind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 470.84,
      "end_seconds": 474.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "You're very welcome. Look after him, Nadia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 476.42,
      "end_seconds": 478.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "I will. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}
